{"name":"Blue Vacation","hex":"#1e7eae","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"vacation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An extended trip or journey away from home for rest or pleasure. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An extended period of leisure time away from work or school."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend or take a vacation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vacation","blocks":[{"text":"A vacation or holiday is either a leave of absence from a regular job or school or an instance of leisure travel away from home. People often take a vacation during specific holiday observances or for specific festivals or celebrations. Vacations are often spent with friends or family. Vacations may include a specific trip or journey, usually for the purpose of recreation or tourism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Vacation_Village_at_Weston_Pool%2C_Weston%2C_Florida_February_24%2C_2022_B.jpg/330px-Vacation_Village_at_Weston_Pool%2C_Weston%2C_Florida_February_24%2C_2022_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vacation"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png/500px-Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png/1280px-Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png/500px-Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Average number of vacation days over time in various countries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADays-of-vacation-and-holidays.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vacation_research_design.jpg/500px-Vacation_research_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vacation_research_design.jpg/1280px-Vacation_research_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vacation_research_design.jpg/500px-Vacation_research_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vacati